    description: "All other major hypergumbo subcommands have --json or --format json (config, search, symbols, slice via --out, compact, dead-code-maybe, io-boundaries, verify-claims, test-coverage). cache-status only produces plain text output: 'Cache directory: /path | Entries: N | Total size: X | Age range: 0-1 days'. Repro: hypergumbo cache-status --json -> exit 2, 'unrecognized arguments: --json'. Found in dogfooding pass 9 (2026-05-28). Same class as 'routes --json' / 'cache-status --json' gaps noted in pass-8 candidates. Programmatic consumers (CI cleanup scripts, dashboards) can't introspect cache state. Suggested fix: add --json flag that emits {cache_dir, entries: [{repo_id, size_bytes, age_days, entry_count}], total_size_bytes, total_entries, honk_threshold_gb}."  # 927e
    fields: {}  # 927e
